.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
Defines a pluggable search strategy for use with the \fRSearch\fP object\&. 

Defines a minimal comparison strategy for two values of type \fIT\fP \&.

.PP
A search provider encapsulates the lookup logic and can implement any strategy: linear scan, binary search, segmented search, pattern matching, or domain‑specific evaluation\&.

.PP
The provider receives the container by reference to allow efficient access without copying\&. It never modifies the container\&.

.PP
\fBTemplate Parameters\fP
.RS 4
\fITContainer\fP The container type implementing \fBIVector<T>\fP\&. 
.br
\fIT\fP The element type stored in the container\&. 
.RE
.PP

.PP
Implementations provide a single boolean comparison operation, allowing containers, sorting policies, and search utilities to determine ordering or equivalence without requiring full IComparer<T> or IComparable<T> semantics\&.

.PP
\fBTemplate Parameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIT\fP The type of elements being compared\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SH "Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "\fBCompareResult\fP SystemEx\&.Algorithms\&.ICompared< T >\&.Compare (Optional< T > x, Optional< T > y)"

.PP
Compares two values and returns a \fBCompareResult\fP indicating whether \fIx\fP  is smaller, larger, or equal to \fIy\fP \&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIx\fP The first value to compare\&.
.br
\fIy\fP The second value to compare\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
A \fBCompareResult\fP describing the ordering relationship between the two values\&. 
.RE
.PP

.PP
Implemented in \fBSystemEx\&.Algorithms\&.SimpleComparer< T >\fP, and \fBSystemEx\&.Algorithms\&.ValueComparer< T >\fP\&.
.PP
Referenced by \fBSystemEx\&.Algorithms\&.BinarySearcherProvider< T, TContainer >\&.Find()\fP, \fBSystemEx\&.Algorithms\&.FibonacciSearcherProvider< T, TContainer >\&.Find()\fP, and \fBSystemEx\&.Algorithms\&.LinearSearchProvider< T, TContainer >\&.Find()\fP\&.
.SS "\fBTriple\fP SystemEx\&.Algorithms\&.ISimpleCompare< T >\&.Compare (Optional< T > a, Optional< T > b)"

.PP
Compares two values and returns \fRtrue\fP if the comparison condition defined by the implementation holds; otherwise \fRfalse\fP\&. The meaning of “comparison condition” depends on the specific comparer: 
.PD 0
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBGreater<T>\fP returns \fRtrue\fP if \fIa\fP  is strictly greater than \fIb\fP \&.  
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBLess<T>\fP returns \fRtrue\fP if \fIa\fP  is strictly less than \fIb\fP \&.  
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBEqualTo<T>\fP returns \fRtrue\fP if both values are equal\&.  
.PP

.PP
Comparers may define additional rules for handling empty or null optionals, depending on the semantics required by the container or algorithm\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIa\fP The first value to compare\&.
.br
\fIb\fP The second value to compare\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
\fRtrue\fP if the comparison condition is satisfied; otherwise \fRfalse\fP\&. 
.RE
.PP

.PP
Implemented in \fBSystemEx\&.Algorithms\&.EqualTo< T >\fP, \fBSystemEx\&.Algorithms\&.Greater< T >\fP, \fBSystemEx\&.Algorithms\&.GreaterEqual< T >\fP, \fBSystemEx\&.Algorithms\&.KleeneEqual< T >\fP, \fBSystemEx\&.Algorithms\&.KleenEqualTo< T >\fP, \fBSystemEx\&.Algorithms\&.KleenGreater< T >\fP, \fBSystemEx\&.Algorithms\&.KleenLess< T >\fP, \fBSystemEx\&.Algorithms\&.Less< T >\fP, \fBSystemEx\&.Algorithms\&.LessEqual< T >\fP, \fBSystemEx\&.Algorithms\&.NetStdCompare< T >\fP, and \fBSystemEx\&.Algorithms\&.NotEqualTo< T >\fP\&.
.PP
Referenced by \fBSystemEx\&.Collections\&.Generic\&.IteratorUtils\&.Find< T >()\fP, \fBSystemEx\&.Collections\&.Generic\&.Find< T, TContainer >\&.LowerBound()\fP, \fBSystemEx\&.Numeric\&.BigDecimal\&.MinMax()\fP, \fBSystemEx\&.Collections\&.Generic\&.Find< T, TContainer >\&.UpperBound()\fP, and \fBSystemEx\&.Collections\&.Generic\&.VectorMultiSet< T, TContainer >\&.Validate()\fP\&.
.SS "long SystemEx\&.Algorithms\&.ISearchProvider< T, TContainer >\&.Find (ref TContainer container, Func< Optional< T >, \fBCompareResult\fP > func)"

.PP
Searches the container using a custom predicate callback\&. The callback receives each element and a boolean flag that can be used to indicate a match condition\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIcontainer\fP The container to search\&.
.br
\fIfunc\fP A predicate callback invoked for each element\&. The callback receives the element and a boolean indicating whether it matches the desired condition\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The index of the first element for which the callback indicates a match, or -1 if no element satisfies the predicate\&. 
.RE
.PP

.PP
Implemented in \fBSystemEx\&.Algorithms\&.BinarySearcherProvider< T, TContainer >\fP, \fBSystemEx\&.Algorithms\&.FibonacciSearcherProvider< T, TContainer >\fP, and \fBSystemEx\&.Algorithms\&.LinearSearchProvider< T, TContainer >\fP\&.
.SS "long SystemEx\&.Algorithms\&.ISearchProvider< T, TContainer >\&.Find (ref TContainer container, ICompared< T > comp, T value)"

.PP
Searches the container for the specified value using the provider's lookup strategy\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIcontainer\fP The container to search\&.
.br
\fIvalue\fP The value to locate\&.
.br
\fIcomp\fP The comparer
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The index of the first matching element, or -1 if no match is found\&. 
.RE
.PP

.PP
Implemented in \fBSystemEx\&.Algorithms\&.BinarySearcherProvider< T, TContainer >\fP, and \fBSystemEx\&.Algorithms\&.FibonacciSearcherProvider< T, TContainer >\fP\&.
.SS "Vector< Pair< long, Optional< T > > > SystemEx\&.Algorithms\&.ISearchProvider< T, TContainer >\&.Where (ref TContainer container, Func< Optional< T >, \fBCompareResult\fP > func)"

.PP
Performs a full linear scan over the container and returns all elements that satisfy the given predicate together with their positions\&. Unlike \fRFind\fP, which only returns the number of matches, \fRWhere\fP provides detailed match information\&. Each result contains both the index of the element inside the container and the element itself\&. This is especially useful when \fIT\fP  is a reference type and positional context is required\&. 

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIcontainer\fP The container to search\&.
.br
\fIfunc\fP Predicate used to test each element\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
A \fBVector<T>\fP containing all matching elements\&. Each pair stores: 
.PD 0
.IP "\(bu" 2
The index of the element in the container 
.IP "\(bu" 2
The element itself 
.PP
.RE
.PP

.PP
Implemented in \fBSystemEx\&.Algorithms\&.BinarySearcherProvider< T, TContainer >\fP, \fBSystemEx\&.Algorithms\&.FibonacciSearcherProvider< T, TContainer >\fP, and \fBSystemEx\&.Algorithms\&.LinearSearchProvider< T, TContainer >\fP\&.
